.TH SIMPLE_SHELL 1 "December 2025" "version 1.0" "Simple Shell Manual"

.SH NAME
simple_shell \- a minimal UNIX command line interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.br
.B echo "command" | ./hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBSimple Shell\fP is a basic UNIX command interpreter written in C.
.br
It displays a prompt, reads user input, parses commands, and executes programs using system calls.
.br
The shell supports both interactive and non-interactive modes. 
.br
In interactive mode, the shell waits for user input and executes commands line by line.
.br 
In non-interactive mode, commands are read from standard input.
.br
Command execution relies on process creation using \fBfork\fP, program replacement using \fBexecve\fP,
and synchronization with child processes using \fBwait\fP.
.br
The shell searches for executable files using the \fBPATH\fP environment variable when a command
is not provided with an absolute or relative path.
.br
Built-in commands implemented include:
.br
- \fBexit\fP : exits the shell
.br
- \fBenv\fP : displays the current environment
.br
If a command is not found or cannot be executed, an error message is printed to standard error.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The shell returns \fB0\fP on normal termination.
.br
If an error occurs during execution, a non-zero value may be returned depending on the failure.

.SH EXAMPLES
Start the shell in interactive mode: ./hsh
.br
Execute a command in non-interactive mode: echo "ls -l" | ./hsh

